# Task board

## Note

`Card` is a WRAPPER: it draws a frame and puts whatever it is given inside it. The
`{children}` hole is where the caller's markup goes, and `Style:` is scoped to this
component alone, so its `.card` rules cannot reach anything else on the page.

## Component Card (title: Text)
Style:
    .card { border: 1px solid #d0d0d0; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px; margin: 8px 0; }
    .card h3 { margin: 0 0 8px 0; font: 600 15px system-ui, sans-serif; }
View:
    <div class="card"><h3>{title}</h3>{children}</div>

## Note

`Row` is a leaf with a CONDITIONAL class. When `done` is false it carries no `done` word
at all — and the served markup says exactly that, which is what lets the pre-rendered
page hydrate without the browser having to correct it.

## Component Row (label: Text) and (done: Bool)
Style:
    .row.done span { text-decoration: line-through; color: #888; }
View:
    <li class="row" class:done={done}><span>{label}</span></li>

## Page /
State:
    Let todos be ["write the parser", "lower the view", "ship it"].
    Let doneCount be 1.
    Let remaining always be (length of todos) - doneCount.
Actions:
    To complete:
        If doneCount is less than (length of todos):
            Set doneCount to doneCount + 1.

    To reset:
        Set doneCount to 0.
View:
    <main>
        <h1>Task board</h1>
        <Card title="This week">
            <ul>
                {for each todo in todos, at index i:}
                    <Row label={todo} done={i is at most doneCount} />
                {end}
            </ul>
            <p id="left">{remaining} left</p>
        </Card>
        <button id="done" on-click={complete}>complete one</button>
        <button id="reset" on-click={reset}>reset</button>
    </main>

## Test: the first task starts done and the count agrees with the rows

Expect that the count of ".row" is equal to 3.
Expect that the count of ".row.done" is equal to 1.
Expect that the text of ".row.done" is equal to "write the parser".
Expect that the text of "#left" is equal to "2 left".

## Test: completing one strikes the next row and counts it down

Click "#done".
Expect that the count of ".row.done" is equal to 2.
Expect that the text of "#left" is equal to "1 left".

## Test: completing stops at the last task

Click "#done".
Click "#done".
Click "#done".
Expect that the count of ".row.done" is equal to 3.
Expect that the text of "#left" is equal to "0 left".

## Test: reset clears every strike

Click "#done".
Click "#reset".
Expect that the count of ".row.done" is equal to 0.
Expect that the text of "#left" is equal to "3 left".

## Test: the card frames the list it was given

Expect that the text of ".card h3" is equal to "This week".
Expect that the count of ".card li" is equal to 3.
